# IdleQuest content lookup (spawn / loot truth)

**Master copy:** keep the fuller agent guidance in sync with
`D:\projects\LustreDamus\.cursor\rules\idlequest-content-lookup.mdc`
(and the EverQuest sample sheets under `D:\projects\LustreDamus\assets\samples\everquest\`).
This LinqPad rule is the slim variant for item-lookup / item-cache / character-tracker work.

Prefer [brynnb/idlequest-content](https://github.com/brynnb/idlequest-content) over P99 wiki alone for spawn and loot.
Wiki is fine for lore; **loot table rows in that repo are what the browser game uses**.

Local clone (when present): `D:\projects\idlequest-content`.

## How to check (no full clone required every time)

Sparse-clone the tables you need into a temp dir:

```powershell
$tmp = Join-Path $env:TEMP "idlequest-content-lookup"
git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/brynnb/idlequest-content.git $tmp
Set-Location $tmp
git sparse-checkout set data/npc_types data/items data/spawn2 data/spawnentry data/spawngroup data/loottable data/loottable_entries data/lootdrop data/lootdrop_entries data/zone
```

Data is hex-sharded `*.ndjson` (one JSON object per line). Names use underscores (`Skeletal_Procurator`); `#` prefixes are common for nameds.

## Join path (from their README / LustreDamus master rule)

```
zone.short_name -> spawn2.zone
spawn2.spawngroupID -> spawnentry.spawngroupID
spawnentry.npcID -> npc_types.id
npc_types.loottable_id -> loottable_entries.loottable_id
loottable_entries.lootdrop_id -> lootdrop_entries.lootdrop_id
lootdrop_entries.item_id -> items.id
```

**Reverse (item → zones)** for `item-cache.json`:

1. `item_id` in `data/lootdrop_entries/` → `lootdrop_id`
2. that `lootdrop_id` in `data/loottable_entries/` → `loottable_id`
3. that `loottable_id` on `data/npc_types/` → NPC `id`
4. that NPC `id` in `data/spawnentry/` → `spawngroupID`
5. that group in `data/spawn2/` → `zone` (short_name)
6. `data/zone/` row with matching `short_name` → prefer storing **`zone.id`** (and optionally `short_name` / `zoneidnumber`) on the cached item

Howling Stones short name: **`charasis`**.

## Practical grep order (item-centric)

1. **Item** — `Select-String data/items/*.ndjson -Pattern '"Name":"…"'` → `id`, stats.
2. **Who drops it** — `'"item_id":<id>,'` in `data/lootdrop_entries/` → `lootdrop_id` + `chance`.
3. **Which loot tables** — that `lootdrop_id` in `data/loottable_entries/` → `loottable_id`.
4. **Which NPCs** — `'"loottable_id":<id>,'` in `data/npc_types/` → `name`, `level`, `id`.
5. **Where they spawn** — `'"npcID":<id>,'` in `data/spawnentry/` → `spawngroupID`; then `data/spawn2/` for `zone` short names → resolve ids via `data/zone/`.

## Gotchas

IdleQuest loot can diverge from P99 wiki attributions (see examples in the LustreDamus master rule). When filling item-cache zone lists, trust the content DB join, not wiki-only drop notes.
